&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;About &lt;strong&gt;Zscaler&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zscaler accelerates digital transformation to ensure our customers can be more agile, efficient, resilient, and secure. As an &lt;strong&gt;AI-forward enterprise&lt;/strong&gt;, we are constantly pushing the envelope, leveraging the world’s largest security data lake to power our cloud-native Zero Trust Exchange platform. This innovation protects our customers from cyberattacks and data loss by securely connecting users, devices, and applications in any location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here, &lt;strong&gt;impact in your role matters more than title&lt;/strong&gt; and trust is built on results. We say, impact over activity. We seek innovators who actively use AI to amplify their impact and who thrive in an environment where we leverage intelligent systems to stay ahead of evolving threats. We believe in transparency and value &lt;strong&gt;constructive, honest debate&lt;/strong&gt;—we’re focused on getting to the best ideas, faster. We build high-performing teams that can make an impact quickly and with high quality. To do this, we are building a culture of execution centered on &lt;strong&gt;customer obsession&lt;/strong&gt;, collaboration, ownership, and accountability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value high-impact, high-accountability with a sense of urgency where you’re enabled to do your best work and embrace your potential. If you’re driven by purpose, thrive on solving complex challenges, and want to be part of the team that’s helping to secure the AI age, we invite you to bring your talents to Zscaler and help shape the future of cybersecurity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Director, People Business Partner - Technology&lt;/strong&gt; to join our Business Partner department in our People &amp;amp; Culture Organization. This role is based in Santa Clara, CA (onsite Tuesday-Thursday) and reports to the VP of HR Business Partnering. As a strategic talent architect for our global Technology organization, you will partner directly with executive leadership to design and scale an organizational structure that fuels innovation. This is a high-impact leadership position requiring the executive presence to influence tech roadmaps and the analytical rigor to solve complex organizational challenges before they become roadblocks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do (Role Expectations)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a critical thought partner to tech executives across AI, Product, Engineering, Innovation and CISO ensuring the talent strategy is inextricably linked to the product and engineering roadmap and workforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose organizational health metrics and sentiment to gauge effectiveness and lead large-scale design initiatives that improve velocity, clarity, and innovation across global teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage advanced data analytics and AI-driven tools to provide high-value talent and leadership insights, moving beyond historical reporting to forecast future business and talent needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive executive-level succession planning, leadership coaching and development, and performance culture designed to thrive in high-velocity technical environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a strategic translator, independently driving high-impact collaboration across P&amp;amp;C Centers of Excellence and cross-functional partners to ensure the unique needs of the Technology org are seamlessly supported&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are (Success Profile)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You act like an owner.&lt;/strong&gt; Your passion for the mission fuels your bias for action. You operate with integrity because you genuinely care about the outcome. You adapt to what’s needed, navigating seamlessly between high-level strategy and hands-on execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are a high-trust collaborator. &lt;/strong&gt;You are ambitious for the team, not just yourself. You embrace our challenge culture by giving and receiving ongoing feedback—knowing that candor delivered with clarity and respect is the truest form of teamwork and the fastest way to earn trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are a positive force.&lt;/strong&gt; You approach hard problems with constructive energy and a &#39;can-do&#39; spirit that is contagious, inspiring your team to stay focused on the solution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You think at scale.&lt;/strong&gt; You connect your day-to-day work to the larger company mission and think globally. You build solutions, processes, and teams that are not just effective today but are built to last and support a high-growth, global organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are resilient and adaptable.&lt;/strong&gt; You view change as an opportunity and setbacks as temporary. You maintain composure and focus in high-pressure situations, guiding yourself and your team through complexity with a steady, positive hand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking for (Minimum Qualifications)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years experience as a People and Culture Partner or HR Leader in a global, high growth, transformative Security or SaaS organization supporting complex Technology organizations (Engineering, Product, IT, etc)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated &quot;Technical Weight&quot; - you understand the nuances of R&amp;amp;D cycles and the evolving landscape of AI, allowing you to speak the language of tech leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to leverage data analytics to tell compelling stories, using data to justify strategic shifts to a highly skeptical, data-centric executive audience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive presence with the &quot;gravitas&quot; to challenge senior leaders and the empathy to serve as the trusted and compassionate face of People &amp;amp; Culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of independently leading large-scale organizational design initiatives, executive-level succession planning, and navigating complex, global talent challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Will Make You Stand Out (Preferred Qualifications)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience actively modernizing People &amp;amp; Culture practices by identifying and integrating AI-driven tools into daily HR analytics and talent insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in acting as a cross-functional &quot;translator,&quot; successfully bridging the gap between high-velocity engineering cultures and specialized corporate functions (Finance, Legal, Compliance, and HR CoEs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience supporting innovation-heavy teams through rapid scaling or significant structural transformation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
