&lt;p&gt;As an &lt;strong&gt;Information System Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; in our IT Digital Employee department (reporting to the Manager, End User Engineering), you will design, implement, and support Zscaler’s global end-user computing (EUC) environment across Windows, macOS, BYOD, and Mobile platforms. Based in Bangalore, India (Hybrid), you will collaborate with IT, Security, and Platform Engineering teams to build secure, cloud-first workspaces fully aligned to Zero Trust principles—balancing priority operational escalations with high-value engineering projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do (Role Expectations)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploy, configure, and maintain corporate-managed endpoints (Windows/macOS/BYOD/Mobile) in alignment with Zscaler security baselines, least-privilege standards, and automated lifecycle workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute vulnerability management workflows using CrowdStrike and Zscaler UVM (Avalor); triage, prioritize, and track risk remediation using Jira, ServiceNow, and executive compliance dashboards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor system performance and user satisfaction using Zscaler Digital Experience (ZDX) and Omnissa, implementing self-healing policies and proactive automation to balance security with productivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate and contribute to complex endpoint issues and security threats, conducting root cause analysis (RCA) and documenting actionable SOPs and runbooks for support teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute for technical initiatives including platform upgrades, virtualization pilots, and security tool rollouts while working cross-functionally across IT Operations, Security, and business leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
