&lt;p&gt;The Zscaler Sales and Go-to-Market team is a global group of professionals who are passionate about delighting our customers, nurturing trusted partnerships, and sharing their expertise to drive a secure, cloud-enabled digital future and further cement our position as the world leader in cloud security. Sales, Customer Success, Sales Enablement, Solution Architects, Business Development, Transformation, and Technology Partnerships all work together to demonstrate the power and agility of Zscaler cloud transformation to the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for an experienced Senior Partner Solution Engineer to join our Global Partner and Partner Engineering team. Reporting to the Senior Manager, Partner Engineering in Japan, you&#39;ll be responsible for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assisting partners in building a robust practice with Zscaler, through the use of education, co-selling activities, partner labs, and service offering creation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working closely with both Zscaler field teams and partner alignment and joint account engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Educating our partners by usage of our training classes and materials, architecture workshops, and other awareness activities with an emphasis on the outcomes those activities can guide&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working closely with the Global GSP, MSSP, and Velocity team members on in theater engagement with these strategic partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What We&#39;re Looking for (Minimum Qualifications)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foundational understanding of AI/ML technologies and experience leveraging, securing, or positioning AI-driven solutions to optimize outcomes within your functional domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of technical pre-sales experience, with professional services or architecture experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broad and deep understanding of security, networking, authentication, and Internet fundamentals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of how to navigate large partner organizational structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building technical champions that influence partner direction and positive outcomes for our partners, Zscaler, and our joint customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated to lead cross-departmental collaboration on strategic initiatives and&amp;nbsp;work on large, complex SaaS solution opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What Will Make You Stand Out (Preferred Qualifications)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing executive-level relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and follow-up skills and engaging interpersonal skills including large scale presentations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Very focused on pipeline development with channel partner engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum Education: Bachelor of Science degree or equivalent work experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel 25% to support partner engagements, industry events, and internal development&lt;/li&gt;
