&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;About &lt;strong&gt;Zscaler&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zscaler accelerates digital transformation to ensure our customers can be more agile, efficient, resilient, and secure. As an &lt;strong&gt;AI-forward enterprise&lt;/strong&gt;, we are constantly pushing the envelope, leveraging the world’s largest security data lake to power our cloud-native Zero Trust Exchange platform. This innovation protects our customers from cyberattacks and data loss by securely connecting users, devices, and applications in any location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here, &lt;strong&gt;impact in your role matters more than title&lt;/strong&gt; and trust is built on results. We say, impact over activity. We seek innovators who actively use AI to amplify their impact and who thrive in an environment where we leverage intelligent systems to stay ahead of evolving threats. We believe in transparency and value &lt;strong&gt;constructive, honest debate&lt;/strong&gt;—we’re focused on getting to the best ideas, faster. We build high-performing teams that can make an impact quickly and with high quality. To do this, we are building a culture of execution centered on &lt;strong&gt;customer obsession&lt;/strong&gt;, collaboration, ownership, and accountability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value high-impact, high-accountability with a sense of urgency where you’re enabled to do your best work and embrace your potential. If you’re driven by purpose, thrive on solving complex challenges, and want to be part of the team that’s helping to secure the AI age, we invite you to bring your talents to Zscaler and help shape the future of cybersecurity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Staff Software Development Engineer to join our team. This is a Hybrid (Mohali) role, reporting to the Director, Software Engineering in the Engineering department. In this position, you will serve as a key technical leader and core development engineer, driving critical system-level optimizations, automation frameworks, and multi-cloud infrastructure strategy across our engineering ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do (Role Expectations)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Linux/FreeBSD-based systems for software development, including configuration and scripting for system-level optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work proficiently across public cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, and GCP) to create and export VM images&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and maintain automation scripts with Python or Shell for infrastructure tasks, system monitoring, and cloud-based workloads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct performance profiling to analyze system performance and identify and troubleshoot resource utilization bottlenecks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with senior engineers to understand, debug, and resolve complex system and application-level issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are (Success Profile)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in ambiguity and build clear paths forward in dynamic environments, viewing complexity as raw material to construct meaningful solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You act like an owner with a strong bias for action and high integrity, seamlessly navigating between high-level strategy and hands-on execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are an energized problem-solver who actively seeks out tough technical challenges to deliver maximum business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a high-trust collaborator who fosters an open challenge culture through constructive candor, mutual respect, and dedication to team success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You embody a true growth mindset, continuously seeking self-development and active feedback to become a stronger partner and teammate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking for (Minimum Qualifications)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated curiosity and active exploration of AI tools, with a proven history of integrating new technologies to enhance daily workflows and augment problem-solving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in C programming with a strong understanding of its core principles and performance optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Python and/or Shell scripting for automation tasks to improve workflow efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid knowledge of Linux/FreeBSD-based operating systems, including process management, threading, memory management, and networking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in working with AWS, Azure, and GCP, including tasks like creating VM images, exporting them, and maintaining infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in designing and maintaining distributed systems, with hands-on experience building, testing, and deploying via Jenkins pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Will Make You Stand Out (Preferred Qualifications)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of networking concepts and protocols, with hands-on experience translating them into system-level solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with database internals, tuning, and optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with version control tools (e.g., Git) for collaborative development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
